* TLS parity for the RDQM app queue manager {{ qm_name }} (#410, #426). Mirrors the
* pcmk mq-pcmk-qmgr MQSC posture: an app-org keystore plus mutual TLS on every
* app-facing channel. The cipher and peer DNs come from the shared tls_* vars
* (group_vars/all/tls.yml -- the #212 seam), so this arm is a keystore-wiring delta,
* not a per-arm channel rewrite.
*
* The keystore lives under the QM's replicated data dir, so SSLKEYR follows the QM on
* every HA node move and the DR cutover. KEYRPWD is persisted in qm.ini (QMs, unlike
* MQI clients, need no sibling .sth stash).
ALTER QMGR SSLKEYR('{{ rdqm_datapath }}/ssl/key') KEYRPWD('{{ pki_keyrpwd.stdout }}') CERTLABL('{{ qm_name }}')
* Real-time monitoring on, so the per-stack mq_prometheus exporter (#423) reports
* channel and queue status -- matching the pcmk/nativeha QMGR posture.
ALTER QMGR MONQ(MEDIUM) MONCHL(MEDIUM) STATMQI(ON) STATQ(ON) STATCHL(MEDIUM) MAXHANDS(512)
* App client -> app QM: mutual TLS, pin the app-org client cert (O=app-org).
ALTER CHANNEL(APP.SVRCONN) CHLTYPE(SVRCONN) SSLCIPH({{ tls_cipher }}) SSLCAUTH(REQUIRED) SSLPEER('{{ tls_peer_client }}')
* Ops exporter -> app QM: the dedicated O=app-org monitoring SVRCONN (#250), new on
* this arm -- the exporter could not previously complete a TLS handshake (#426).
DEFINE CHANNEL(MON.SVRCONN) CHLTYPE(SVRCONN) TRPTYPE(TCP) MCAUSER('mqm') SSLCIPH({{ tls_cipher }}) SSLCAUTH(REQUIRED) SSLPEER('{{ tls_peer_client }}') REPLACE
* Inter-QM link to the SVC counterparty (O=svc-org): SDR + RCVR to mutual TLS, so our
* side stops being both plaintext and mismatched against the TLS-expecting SVC peer (#410).
ALTER CHANNEL({{ chl_to_svc }}) CHLTYPE(SDR) SSLCIPH({{ tls_cipher }}) SSLPEER('{{ tls_peer_svc }}')
ALTER CHANNEL({{ chl_to_app }}) CHLTYPE(RCVR) SSLCIPH({{ tls_cipher }}) SSLCAUTH(REQUIRED) SSLPEER('{{ tls_peer_svc }}')
* Reload the keystore so the new certs take effect on the next channel start.
REFRESH SECURITY TYPE(SSL)
